      "content": "I hear you, but it sounds like you're saying the \"debate\" is mostly just social and not actually scientific. When people bring up those arguments about biological essentialism or the idea that sex is an immutable binary, are those views just dismissed by scientists as being wrong or unscientific? It's hard to tell if there's any actual scientific merit to the criticism or if it's just being labeled as outdated.",
